    "result": "Excellent! All tests are passing now. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n**1. Fixed governance module exports** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\n- Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n- The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export\n\n**2. Fixed toxicity metric signature** (`src/eval/metrics.js`)\n- Changed `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms)` to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references)`\n- The `runEvaluations` function passes both outputs and references to all metrics, but `toxicityMetric` was treating the references as banned terms, causing false positives\n- Now the function ignores the references parameter and always uses the default banned terms\n\nAll 28 tests in frai-core and 11 tests in frai-gate are now passing. The existing public exports remain unchanged and functional.",
